the California parents accused of  holding their 13 children captive will  be in court today for procedural hearing  for the first time lawyers representing  the seven adult children are sharing how  their recovery is going and what their  dreams are for the future  Mireya Villarreal is outside the Paris  California home where the children were  allegedly held Mattea good morning good  morning those children were rescued here  at this home nearly six weeks ago  sources tell CBS News the six younger  siblings are actually living in two  foster homes right now and the seven  older siblings are actually staying at a  nearby Medical Center they are being  exposed to everything from Harry Potter  movies to using an iPad as the legal  case against David and Louise Turpin  moves forward the children they  allegedly imprisoned for years are  moving on with their lives making  decisions on their own for the first  time that in itself is kind of a a new  experience for them understanding that  they do have rights and they do have a  voice Jack Osbourne and Caleb Mason  represent the older siblings they say  the staff at the corona Medical Center  has converted part of the hospital to  make it more comfortable they set up an  outdoor area where they can play sports  and exercise prosecutors say the  siblings spent years in captivity  sometimes chained to their beds severely  underfed but now they're free to make  their own choices that's a big deal I'm  deciding what they're gonna read  deciding what they're gonna wear these  are all things that our decisions they  make every day which are new and and an  empowering Corona mayor Karen Spiegel  works closely with the siblings nurses  there talk about how warm and loving  these kids are and so appreciative some  of them had never really seen a  toothbrush before things that we just  take for granted means so much to these  kids the older and younger siblings have  not yet reunited but they communicate  using Skype in the short-term the  attorneys say the older children simply  want to go to the beach the mountains  and the movies but longer-term they want  to attend college and pursue careers I  just want you to  understand just what special individuals  they are they all have their own  aspirations and their own interests and  now they may have an opportunity to to  address those which is really exciting  the couple has pled not guilty to  multiple counts of child abuse torture  and false imprisonment if this does go  to trial the Riverside County District  Attorney says he does plan to put those  children on the witness stand  bianna hopefully these children who get  a second chance at a normal life Maria  thank you
 

